# vit_v0_default: ViT-Base/16 transfer baseline on the GPU line (not a waterfall row).
#
# reason     SHAFT-CPU-ViT measured the host-pool transfer (2.780x vs BERT 4.057x); this line's BERT
#            reduction is 19.232x VRAM, 1.365x host (GEOMETRY-TRANSFER.md).
# geometry   ViT-Base/16 against BERT-base (checkpoint config):
#              hidden 768, 12 layers, 12 heads, FFN 3072      identical
#              tokens 197 (196 patches + CLS) against 128     geometry
#              Conv2d 16x16x3 patch projection against a 28,996-entry vocabulary lookup
#              no attention mask                              one encrypted operand fewer per layer
#              final LayerNorm + CLS slice, no pooler         head
# setup      no levers. Checkpoint from a bound directory (image has only BERT, nodes offline); sbatch
#            vit_* branch announces VIT_TRANSFER=1. Driver derives tokens = (image_size/patch_size)^2 + 1
#            and exits non-zero if SHAFT_MAX_LENGTH differs.
BASELINE_SCRIPT=$BASE/vit_instrumented_gpu.py
SHAFT_SCRIPT=vit_instrumented_gpu.py
SHAFT_LEVERS=
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_MODEL=/vit SHAFT_MAX_LENGTH=197"
